// Bun Snapshot v1, https://bun.sh/docs/test/snapshots

exports[`layer 0 fits the budget and lists every command once 1`] = `
"meant 0.1.0 — business intent and behavior

A Meant model describes what an application should do.
People decide the behavior; agents help author the model;
engineers choose the implementation. The toolkit checks models deterministically.
Model files: .meant, or \`\`\`meant fences in .md.

Agent bootstrap:
  1. Read \`meant skill\` into context (persist it: \`meant skill install\`).
  2. Loop: edit → \`meant check <model dir> --json\` → fix errors → \`meant fmt <file>\`.
  3. Depth on demand: \`meant check --explain <LAW>\` · \`meant spec <section>\`.
  4. Modeling an existing app: read the "Starting from code" section of \`meant skill\`.

Commands
  check <paths> [--json] [--explain <LAW>]   parse/resolve/laws; exit 1 iff errors
  fmt <paths> [--check]                      canonical form; --check exits 1 on drift
  sim <paths> [--json]                       witness / probe / replay verdicts
  report <paths> [--json]                    opacity, patterns, candidates, questions
  skill [install]                            agent editing discipline (stdout, or write .claude/skills/)
  spec [<section> | --all]                   the normative grammar (TOC by default)
  hook                                       PostToolUse hook: stdin JSON -> diagnostics feedback
"
`;
